0..78 Comment "// An extension type stated as the signature the face theory generates for it."
79..157 Comment "// `ext Val on left is zero` over the two points of `Two` is the type of cells"
158..233 Comment "// fixed to `zero` on the face `left`: a cell holds its value off the face,"
234..312 Comment "// `ins` introduces it and `out0`, `out1` read it at each point. The boundary,"
313..393 Comment "// β and η are the signature\'s laws, so each holds by conversion, on a neutral"
394..471 Comment "// cell as on an introduced one (Tesla Zhang, _Three non-cubical applications"
472..551 Comment "// of extension types_, arXiv:2311.05658). The surface spelling `ext A on φ is"
552..572 Comment "// u` waits on #641."
574..650 Comment "/// The cells of `Val` over `Two` fixed to `zero` on `left`, with `c` a cell"
651..729 Comment "/// nothing introduces. The boundary reads `zero` at `left` of every cell, `c`"
730..809 Comment "/// included; β reads an introduced cell\'s value at the point off the face; η"
810..851 Comment "/// rebuilds a cell from its value there."
852..854 Other "@["
855..865 Other "normalizes"
865..866 Other "("
866..867 StringLit "\""
867..934 StringLit "cells(out0(c), out1(ins(one)), ins(out1(c))) ~> cells(zero, one, c)"
934..935 StringLit "\""
935..936 Other ")"
937..938 Other "]"
